@id: scene.033_the_march
@when: Unknown.scene_033_the_march
@where: Realm/Physical/Unknown
@scope: narrative
@entities: [Kress, Mika, Sera]
@region: Unknown
@environment: wasteland
@terrain_family: wasteland
@spatial_scale_hint: massive

=segments:
  - line: 1
    type: narration
    text: "book 6"
  - line: 2
    type: narration
    text: "chapter 033-the march"
  - line: 4
    type: narration
    text: "~~~CHAPTER 32: \"THE MARCH~~~~"
  - line: 6
    type: narration
    text: "The war camp stank of determination and desperation in equal measure."
  - line: 7
    type: narration
    text: "Mika stood at the edge of the elevated command platform, surveying the assembled remnants of Geralt's army—warriors who'd followed him through impossible battles and somehow survived."
  - line: 8
    type: narration
    text: "They looked at her now with expressions that ranged from hope to skepticism, waiting to see if the woman who'd stood at Geralt's side could lead them through one more impossible mission."
  - line: 10
    type: narration
    text: "She could feel their doubt like a physical weight."
  - line: 11
    type: narration
    text: "And why wouldn't they doubt?"
  - line: 12
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt was gone—transported somewhere by the Needle's malfunction, location unknown, status uncertain."
  - line: 13
    type: narration
    text: "Their legendary leader, the man who'd reshaped continents with his will and magic, had simply... vanished."
  - line: 14
    type: narration
    text: "Leaving her."
  - line: 16
    type: narration
    text: "Mika planted her hands on the platform's railing, feeling the grain of the wood beneath her palms."
  - line: 17
    type: narration
    text: "Real."
  - line: 18
    type: narration
    text: "Solid."
  - line: 19
    type: narration
    text: "Unlike the cosmic forces that had stolen her husband."
  - line: 21
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "\"Listen up,\""
  - line: 23
    type: narration
    text: "She let that hang in the air for a moment, watched it settle into the spaces between soldiers."
  - line: 25
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Here's what I'm thinking.\""
  - line: 26
    type: narration
    text: "Her voice dropped lower, forcing them to lean in, to strain to hear. \"Geralt didn't build this army on fear or obligation. He built it on something simpler: we don't leave our people behind. Ever. Not when they're wounded. Not when they're captured. And sure as hell not when they're lost.\""
  - line: 28
    type: narration
    text: "A few nods in the crowd."
  - line: 29
    type: narration
    text: "Mostly the veterans, the ones who'd been there for the campaigns that had forged this principle into something approaching religion."
  - line: 31
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"He's out there. Somewhere. And he's either fighting his way back to us, or he's waiting for us to find him. Either way, we march.\""
  - line: 32
    type: narration
    text: "She straightened, her voice gaining steel. \"I need volunteers. Fast march, light gear, combat ready. We'll be moving through contested territory with no support. High chance of contact with hostiles. Very high chance of not coming back.\""
  - line: 34
    type: narration
    text: "Silence."
  - line: 35
    type: narration
    text: "The kind that felt like a held breath."
  - line: 37
    type: narration
    text: "Then, from the back of the crowd, a scarred veteran with a prosthetic arm raised his fist."
  - line: 38
    type: narration
    text: "\"Where we going, Commander?\""
  - line: 40
    type: narration
    text: "Mika allowed herself a small, fierce smile."
  - line: 41
    type: narration
    text: "\"Southwest."
  - line: 42
    type: narration
    text: "Toward the crash site."
  - line: 43
    type: narration
    text: "That's where the Needle's energy signature was pointing when Geralt vanished."
  - line: 44
    type: narration
    text: "We find the crash."
  - line: 45
    type: narration
    text: "We find leads."
  - line: 46
    type: narration
    text: "We find him.\""
  - line: 48
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"How many you want?\""
  - line: 49
    type: narration
    text: "This from Lieutenant Kress, one of Geralt's tactical officers—a woman who'd lost an eye in the Battle of Ashren Gate and gained a reputation for refusing to die no matter how creative the universe got about trying to kill her."
  - line: 51
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Mika
    text: "\"Twenty,\""
  - line: 53
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Things always go sideways,\""
  - line: 54
    type: narration
    text: "Kress observed dryly."
  - line: 56
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Exactly. So I want people who are good at it.\""
  - line: 57
    type: narration
    text: "Mika gestured sharply. \"Kress, you're second in command. Pick your specialists. We move in one hour. Light rations, combat loadout, no luxuries.\""
  - line: 59
    type: dialogue
    speaker: someone
    text: "\"What about command here?\""
  - line: 61
    type: narration
    text: "Mika had already considered this."
  - line: 62
    type: narration
    text: "\"Captain Vorren takes temporary command of base operations."
  - line: 63
    type: narration
    text: "Defensive posture."
  - line: 64
    type: narration
    text: "No offensive operations while we're gone."
  - line: 65
    type: narration
    text: "If we're not back in ten days—\" She paused, meeting eyes across the crowd."
  - line: 66
    type: narration
    text: "\"—assume the worst and make your own choices."
  - line: 67
    type: narration
    text: "I won't ask anyone to die for a lost cause.\""
  - line: 69
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Ten days,\""
  - line: 70
    type: narration
    text: "Kress repeated, her tone making it clear what she thought of that timeline."
  - line: 72
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Ten days to march to the crash site, search it, and get back. Tight, but doable if we push.\""
  - line: 73
    type: narration
    text: "Mika's jaw set. \"I'm not leaving him out there longer than that.\""
  - line: 75
    type: narration
    text: "The crowd dispersed with the kind of purposeful energy that came from having clear orders after uncertainty."
  - line: 76
    type: narration
    text: "Mika watched them go, then descended from the platform to begin her own preparations."
  - line: 78
    type: narration
    text: "She found her armor where she'd left it—Dragon Armor, the same type Geralt wore, though hers was lighter, designed for speed rather than raw protection."
  - line: 79
    type: narration
    text: "The scales gleamed dully in the afternoon light, each one a masterwork of Anunnaki engineering that Geralt had... liberated... during one of their more legally questionable operations."
  - line: 81
    type: narration
    text: "She ran her fingers over the scales, remembering the day he'd given it to her."
  - line: 82
    type: narration
    text: "\"If you're going to insist on following me into suicide missions,\" he'd said, that particular mix of exasperation and affection in his voice, \"at least do it in gear that might keep you alive.\""
  - line: 84
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Miss him?\""
  - line: 85
    type: narration
    text: "a voice asked from behind her."
  - line: 87
    type: narration
    text: "Mika didn't turn, recognizing Sera's voice—the combat mage who specialized in defensive wards and had saved Mika's life more times than either of them bothered counting anymore."
  - line: 88
    type: narration
    text: "\"Every minute he's gone is a minute something could be killing him.\""
  - line: 90
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Could be,\""
  - line: 91
    type: narration
    text: "Sera agreed, moving to stand beside her. \"Could also be he's fine. Geralt's hard to kill. Universe has tried repeatedly. Results remain inconclusive.\""
  - line: 93
    type: narration
    text: "Despite everything, Mika smiled."
  - line: 94
    type: narration
    text: "\"You volunteering for the march?\""
  - line: 96
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Obviously. Someone needs to keep you from doing anything stupid.\""
  - line: 97
    type: narration
    text: "Sera paused. \"Anything *unnecessarily* stupid. The necessarily stupid is unavoidable at this point.\""
  - line: 99
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Fair assessment.\""
  - line: 101
    type: narration
    text: "They geared up in comfortable silence, the kind that came from years of fighting side by side."
  - line: 102
    type: narration
    text: "Mika strapped on her armor piece by piece, feeling the weight settle onto her shoulders like purpose made tangible."
  - line: 103
    type: narration
    text: "Sera checked her focus crystals, the gems glowing softly with stored magical energy."
  - line: 105
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Sera
    text: "\"Question,\""
  - line: 107
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Then we expand the search.\""
  - line: 108
    type: narration
    text: "Mika's voice was flat, brooking no argument. \"We check every settlement, every outpost, every gods-damned cave within a hundred miles if we have to.\""
  - line: 110
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"And if we run into whoever caused the crash? Because someone knocked that ship out of the sky, and I'm guessing they're not friendly.\""
  - line: 112
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Then they get to explain themselves.\""
  - line: 113
    type: narration
    text: "Mika's hand moved to her sword hilt. \"Briefly. Right before they stop breathing.\""
  - line: 115
    type: narration
    text: "Sera grinned, sharp and dangerous."
  - line: 116
    type: narration
    text: "\"There's the commander I know.\""
  - line: 118
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 120
    type: narration
    text: "The assembled strike force looked exactly like what Mika had requested: twenty of the most dangerous individuals who'd ever had the poor judgment to follow Geralt into battle."
  - line: 121
    type: narration
    text: "Scouts who could move through hostile territory like ghosts."
  - line: 122
    type: narration
    text: "Combat mages with enough raw power to level buildings."
  - line: 123
    type: narration
    text: "Heavy infantry who treated \"impossible odds\" as a suggestion rather than a deterrent."
  - line: 125
    type: narration
    text: "Kress had outdone herself with the selections."
  - line: 126
    type: narration
    text: "Mika recognized most of them—veterans of campaigns that had become legend, survivors of battles that had killed everyone around them."
  - line: 127
    type: narration
    text: "The kind of soldiers who didn't flinch when orders included phrases like \"probably suicidal.\""
  - line: 129
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Listen up,\""
  - line: 130
    type: narration
    text: "Mika addressed them, her voice carrying the command presence she'd learned from watching Geralt. \"This is a rescue operation. Priority one: find Geralt. Priority two: survive. Everything else is negotiable. We move fast, we move quiet, and we move *smart*. Questions?\""
  - line: 132
    type: narration
    text: "A scout raised his hand—Talven, a man whose face was more scar tissue than skin after an unfortunate encounter with a fire elemental."
  - line: 133
    type: narration
    text: "\"Rules of engagement?\""
  - line: 135
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Avoid contact when possible. When impossible, end it quickly and keep moving. We're not here to fight a war. We're here to find one man and bring him home.\""
  - line: 137
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"What if he's—\""
  - line: 138
    type: narration
    text: "someone started."
  - line: 140
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"He's alive,\""
  - line: 141
    type: narration
    text: "Mika cut them off, her voice harder than forged steel. \"And we're bringing him back. Anyone who has a problem with that certainty can stay here.\""
  - line: 143
    type: narration
    text: "No one moved."
  - line: 145
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Good. We march in five. Check your gear, check your buddy, and prepare for a week of pain.\""
  - line: 146
    type: narration
    text: "She paused, then added with a hint of grim humor, \"The good news is, if we all die horribly, at least we'll have died doing something stupid for a good reason. Geralt would appreciate that.\""
  - line: 148
    type: narration
    text: "A ripple of dark laughter moved through the group."
  - line: 149
    type: narration
    text: "They were ready."
  - line: 151
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 153
    type: narration
    text: "They left the camp as the sun reached its zenith, moving in a loose formation that could tighten into defensive positions at a moment's notice."
  - line: 154
    type: narration
    text: "Mika took point with the scouts, Kress anchoring the rear with the heavy infantry, combat mages distributed throughout to provide support wherever fighting erupted."
  - line: 156
    type: narration
    text: "The terrain shifted quickly from the settled farmlands around the camp to wild country—forests that hadn't seen human management in generations, hills that rose and fell with no regard for convenient travel routes."
  - line: 157
    type: narration
    text: "They made good time despite the rough ground, pushing a pace that would have broken less conditioned forces."
  - line: 159
    type: narration
    text: "By evening of the first day, they'd covered thirty miles."
  - line: 161
    type: narration
    text: "They made cold camp in a defensible ravine, no fires to give away their position."
  - line: 162
    type: narration
    text: "Mika sat with her back against stone, chewing dried meat that tasted like leather and regret, while Kress reviewed tomorrow's route by the dim light of a hooded glow-crystal."
  - line: 164
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"We'll hit the contested zone around midday tomorrow,\""
  - line: 165
    type: narration
    text: "Kress observed, tracing a finger along the crude map. \"The area between the Ashren territories and the Broken Kingdoms. Neither side controls it effectively, which means both sides send patrols through.\""
  - line: 167
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"How recent is this intelligence?\""
  - line: 169
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Two weeks old. Could be completely different now.\""
  - line: 170
    type: narration
    text: "Kress shrugged. \"Could be the same. Either way, expect contact.\""
  - line: 172
    type: narration
    text: "Mika studied the map, calculating routes and fallback positions."
  - line: 173
    type: narration
    text: "\"We skirt the eastern edge."
  - line: 174
    type: narration
    text: "More broken terrain, harder to march through, but less likely to run into organized patrols.\""
  - line: 176
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"More likely to run into bandits, though.\""
  - line: 178
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I'll take bandits over trained soldiers any day. Bandits run when the fighting gets hard.\""
  - line: 180
    type: narration
    text: "Kress snorted."
  - line: 181
    type: narration
    text: "\"These bandits clearly haven't heard about us.\""
  - line: 183
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Then they'll learn.\""
  - line: 184
    type: narration
    text: "Mika rolled her shoulders, feeling the Dragon Armor flex with the motion. \"Get some sleep, Lieutenant. Tomorrow gets interesting.\""
  - line: 186
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Tomorrow's always interesting with you, Commander.\""
  - line: 187
    type: narration
    text: "But Kress moved off to find her bedroll, leaving Mika alone with the night and her thoughts."
  - line: 189
    type: narration
    text: "She stared up at the stars, wondering if Geralt could see them too, wherever he was."
  - line: 190
    type: narration
    text: "Wondering if he was scared, or hurt, or fighting."
  - line: 191
    type: narration
    text: "Probably fighting."
  - line: 192
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt's answer to most problems involved hitting them until they stopped being problems."
  - line: 194
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "\"Hang on,\""
  - line: 196
    type: narration
    text: "The stars, as usual, declined to comment."
  - line: 198
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 200
    type: narration
    text: "Contact came, as predicted, midday of the second day."
  - line: 202
    type: narration
    text: "They were moving through a narrow valley, steep hills rising on either side, when Talven raised a fist—the signal for halt."
  - line: 203
    type: narration
    text: "The column froze instantly, every soldier dropping into combat-ready positions without needing orders."
  - line: 205
    type: narration
    text: "Mika moved forward in a crouch, joining the scout at the head of the column."
  - line: 206
    type: narration
    text: "\"What've you got?\""
  - line: 208
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Movement. Ridge line, eleven o'clock.\""
  - line: 209
    type: narration
    text: "Talven pointed with two fingers. \"At least a dozen, maybe more. Military formation, but the gear's mixed. Could be mercenaries. Could be deserters turned bandit.\""
  - line: 211
    type: narration
    text: "Mika studied the ridge through narrowed eyes."
  - line: 212
    type: narration
    text: "She could just make out figures moving along the crest, silhouetted against the afternoon sky."
  - line: 213
    type: narration
    text: "\"They've seen us?\""
  - line: 215
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Probably. We're not exactly stealthy with twenty bodies.\""
  - line: 216
    type: narration
    text: "Talven's scarred face twisted into something that might have been a smile. \"They're deciding if we're worth the trouble.\""
  - line: 218
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Show them we're not.\""
  - line: 219
    type: narration
    text: "Mika raised her voice just loud enough to carry to her troops. \"Combat formation. Defensive posture. We're not looking for a fight, but we're ready to finish one. Mages, light up your crystals. Let them see what they're dealing with.\""
  - line: 221
    type: narration
    text: "The column shifted smoothly into a defensive wedge, combat mages stepping forward with focus crystals blazing."
  - line: 222
    type: narration
    text: "The message was clear: we're strong, we're organized, and we really don't have time for your bullshit."
  - line: 224
    type: narration
    text: "For a long moment, nothing happened."
  - line: 225
    type: narration
    text: "The figures on the ridge remained still, presumably having their own discussion about risk versus reward."
  - line: 227
    type: narration
    text: "Then they withdrew, melting back from the ridge line."
  - line: 229
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Smart,\""
  - line: 230
    type: narration
    text: "Kress observed, moving up to join Mika. \"They recognized military discipline when they saw it.\""
  - line: 232
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Or they're flanking us.\""
  - line: 233
    type: narration
    text: "Mika scanned the surrounding terrain with the paranoia that had kept her alive through a dozen campaigns. \"Double the scouts. Eyes on all approaches. We keep moving, but we move ready.\""
  - line: 235
    type: narration
    text: "They pushed through the valley without further incident, but Mika felt eyes on them for hours afterward."
  - line: 236
    type: narration
    text: "The contested zone was living up to its reputation—too many armed groups with too many competing interests, all trying to carve out territory in the chaos left by larger conflicts."
  - line: 238
    type: narration
    text: "By the third day, they'd entered truly wild country."
  - line: 239
    type: narration
    text: "The vegetation grew thicker, older, with trees that had stood for centuries and showed no interest in accommodating human passage."
  - line: 240
    type: narration
    text: "Progress slowed as scouts had to find viable routes through terrain that actively resisted travel."
  - line: 242
    type: narration
    text: "It was during a rest break, with the column strung out along a game trail barely wide enough for single file, that the real trouble found them."
  - line: 244
    type: narration
    text: "Sera was the first to sense it."
  - line: 245
    type: narration
    text: "\"Magic,\" she hissed, her focus crystals flaring."
  - line: 246
    type: narration
    text: "\"Big."
  - line: 247
    type: narration
    text: "Incoming!\""
  - line: 249
    type: narration
    text: "Mika's hand went to her sword."
  - line: 250
    type: narration
    text: "\"Direction?\""
  - line: 252
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Everywhere!\""
  - line: 253
    type: narration
    text: "Sera's eyes went wide. \"It's not targeted—it's ambient. Something's charging the atmosphere with—\""
  - line: 255
    type: narration
    text: "The forest exploded."
  - line: 257
    type: narration
    text: "Not with fire or force, but with *growth*."
  - line: 258
    type: narration
    text: "Vines erupted from the soil like striking serpents, wrapping around boots and legs."
  - line: 259
    type: narration
    text: "Trees bent and twisted, branches reaching with predatory intent."
  - line: 260
    type: narration
    text: "The ground itself seemed to writhe, roots breaking through soil to entangle the column."
  - line: 262
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Nature magic!\""
  - line: 263
    type: narration
    text: "Kress roared over the chaos. \"Someone's weaponizing the fucking forest!\""
  - line: 265
    type: narration
    text: "Mika cut through a vine that had wrapped around her calf, the Dragon Armor's enchantments protecting her from the worst of the attack."
  - line: 266
    type: narration
    text: "\"Combat mages!"
  - line: 267
    type: narration
    text: "Counterspell!"
  - line: 268
    type: narration
    text: "Everyone else, cut yourselves free and get to high ground!\""
  - line: 270
    type: narration
    text: "Sera and the other combat mages began chanting, their combined power pushing back against the nature magic assault."
  - line: 271
    type: narration
    text: "The wild growth slowed, stopped, began to recede—but the damage was done."
  - line: 272
    type: narration
    text: "The column was scattered, soldiers fighting individual battles against an enemy that was literally the ground beneath their feet."
  - line: 274
    type: narration
    text: "And then the real attackers struck."
  - line: 276
    type: narration
    text: "They came from the trees—figures wrapped in living bark and leaves, moving with inhuman speed."
  - line: 277
    type: narration
    text: "Not quite human, not quite plant, something in between that spoke to magic gone wrong or deliberately twisted."
  - line: 278
    type: narration
    text: "Druids?"
  - line: 279
    type: narration
    text: "Nature wardens?"
  - line: 280
    type: narration
    text: "Mika didn't know and didn't care."
  - line: 282
    type: narration
    text: "She met the first attacker head-on, her sword flashing in a perfectly executed arc that should have severed the creature at the waist."
  - line: 283
    type: narration
    text: "Instead, the blade bit into wood-like flesh and stuck, caught in fiber that was stronger than it looked."
  - line: 285
    type: narration
    text: "The creature's arm lashed out, catching Mika across the chest."
  - line: 286
    type: narration
    text: "The Dragon Armor absorbed most of the impact, but the force still sent her staggering."
  - line: 288
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "\"They're tough!\""
  - line: 290
    type: narration
    text: "The battle dissolved into chaos."
  - line: 291
    type: narration
    text: "Mika found herself fighting beside Sera, the combat mage's defensive wards keeping them alive while Mika's blade slowly dismantled their attackers."
  - line: 292
    type: narration
    text: "Around them, the rest of the column fought similar desperate actions, small groups of soldiers holding defensive positions against creatures that seemed to reform even as they were cut down."
  - line: 294
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"This is insane!\""
  - line: 295
    type: narration
    text: "Sera panted, maintaining a ward that had just deflected what looked like a spear made of thorns. \"Why are we being attacked by angry trees?\""
  - line: 297
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"We're trespassing,\""
  - line: 298
    type: narration
    text: "Mika grunted, her sword finally finding a weak point in her opponent's wooden armor. The creature collapsed, leaves scattering. \"This forest is someone's territory. We just walked in without asking permission.\""
  - line: 300
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Little busy for etiquette lessons!\""
  - line: 302
    type: narration
    text: "A new figure emerged from the tree line—taller than the others, crowned with antlers that might have been bone or might have been living wood."
  - line: 303
    type: narration
    text: "Its voice resonated with harmonics that suggested it was speaking multiple languages simultaneously, only one of which was comprehensible to human ears."
  - line: 305
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Trespassers. Despoilers. You bring war-stink into sacred groves. You will feed the soil.\""
  - line: 307
    type: narration
    text: "Mika spat blood, faced the newcomer with her sword raised."
  - line: 308
    type: narration
    text: "\"We're passing through."
  - line: 309
    type: narration
    text: "We're not here to fight you or damage your forest."
  - line: 310
    type: narration
    text: "Let us pass and we'll be gone by nightfall.\""
  - line: 312
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"All who bear weapons despoil. All who march in formation bring war. The forest will reclaim what humanity stole.\""
  - line: 313
    type: narration
    text: "The antlered figure raised its arms, and the forest responded—trees groaning as they leaned inward, cutting off escape routes."
  - line: 315
    type: narration
    text: "Mika made a calculation."
  - line: 316
    type: narration
    text: "They could fight."
  - line: 317
    type: narration
    text: "Probably win—combat mages could level the forest if they had to."
  - line: 318
    type: narration
    text: "But it would cost time, resources, and possibly lives."
  - line: 319
    type: narration
    text: "And they were still days from the crash site."
  - line: 321
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "\"Sera,\""
  - line: 323
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Enough for what you're thinking, if you're thinking something suitably dramatic.\""
  - line: 325
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Always am.\""
  - line: 326
    type: narration
    text: "Mika raised her voice, addressing the antlered druid. \"You want us gone? Fine. But we're not walking. Sera—portal. Now.\""
  - line: 328
    type: narration
    text: "The combat mage didn't hesitate."
  - line: 329
    type: narration
    text: "Her hands moved in complex patterns, focus crystals blazing as she tore a hole in reality itself."
  - line: 330
    type: narration
    text: "Portal magic was dangerous, unpredictable, and absolutely forbidden by most magical authorities for good reasons."
  - line: 331
    type: narration
    text: "But Sera had never been much for following rules, and desperate times called for desperate measures."
  - line: 333
    type: narration
    text: "Space ripped open with a sound like tearing fabric, revealing a shimmering doorway that showed a landscape miles away."
  - line: 335
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Everyone through!\""
  - line: 336
    type: narration
    text: "Mika commanded. \"Move!\""
  - line: 338
    type: narration
    text: "The column didn't need to be told twice."
  - line: 339
    type: narration
    text: "Soldiers dove through the portal in pairs, disappearing from the forest."
  - line: 340
    type: narration
    text: "The antlered druid roared in fury, but Sera's wards held against the renewed assault of nature magic."
  - line: 342
    type: narration
    text: "Mika was last through, Sera right behind her, and the portal snapped closed just as a massive root smashed through the space where they'd been standing."
  - line: 344
    type: narration
    text: "They tumbled out onto rocky ground under open sky, the forest left behind, several miles covered in seconds."
  - line: 345
    type: narration
    text: "The column sprawled around them, gasping, bleeding, but intact."
  - line: 347
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Mika
    text: "\"Everyone accounted for?\""
  - line: 349
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"All present,\""
  - line: 350
    type: narration
    text: "Kress confirmed after a quick head count. \"Some injuries, nothing critical. Though Talven's probably going to complain about his ankle for the next three days.\""
  - line: 352
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"He can complain all he wants as long as he can still scout.\""
  - line: 353
    type: narration
    text: "Mika looked around, orienting herself. The portal had dropped them near a series of low hills. In the distance, she could see smoke staining the sky. \"That's it. The crash site.\""
  - line: 355
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"We're close,\""
  - line: 356
    type: narration
    text: "Sera observed, her focus crystals dim now, power exhausted. \"Maybe ten miles out.\""
  - line: 358
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Then we rest here for two hours, tend injuries, and push for the crash site before dark.\""
  - line: 359
    type: narration
    text: "Mika sheathed her sword, feeling the weight of exhaustion settling into her bones. Three days of forced march and a magical battle. But they were close."
  - line: 361
    type: narration
    text: "She could feel it in her bones: Geralt was near."
  - line: 362
    type: narration
    text: "They just had to find him among the wreckage of whatever catastrophe had brought that ship down."
  - line: 364
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Rest up,\""
  - line: 365
    type: narration
    text: "she told her troops. \"The easy part's over. The hard part starts when we reach the crash site and find out what knocked a ship that size out of the sky.\""
  - line: 367
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Kress
    text: "\"Any theories?\""
  - line: 369
    type: narration
    text: "Mika studied the distant smoke, her jaw tight."
  - line: 370
    type: narration
    text: "\"Theories are for people with time."
  - line: 371
    type: narration
    text: "We get there, we assess, we find Geralt, we leave."
  - line: 372
    type: narration
    text: "Everything else is someone else's problem.\""
  - line: 374
    type: narration
    text: "The column settled in to rest, but Mika remained standing, staring at that pillar of smoke."
  - line: 375
    type: narration
    text: "Somewhere in that wreckage, her husband was either fighting to survive or waiting to be rescued."
  - line: 377
    type: narration
    text: "Either way, she was coming."
  - line: 379
    type: narration
    text: "The universe had made a mistake taking him."
  - line: 380
    type: narration
    text: "She was going to correct it."
  - line: 382
    type: narration
    text: "Violently, if necessary."
  - line: 384
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 385
    type: narration
    text: "The old igigi compass spun wildly, its needle pointing at everything except north."
  - line: 386
    type: narration
    text: "Mika kicked it into the canyon's dust."
  - line: 387
    type: narration
    text: "\"We're going that way,\" she declared, gesturing toward the unnatural tear in the mountains ahead."
  - line: 389
    type: narration
    text: "Two hundred and fifty pairs of boots crunched over shattered rock."
  - line: 390
    type: narration
    text: "The Anunnaki ship hadn't landed; it had carved its tomb."
  - line: 391
    type: narration
    text: "Twenty miles of armored hull lay crumpled against the peaks, plowing valleys where none existed yesterday."
  - line: 392
    type: narration
    text: "Jagged metal cliffs rose higher than cathedrals, dripping coolant like black blood."
  - line: 393
    type: narration
    text: "The air reeked of scorched earth and something disturbingly sweet."
  - line: 395
    type: narration
    text: "They climbed the wreck’s lower slopes."
  - line: 396
    type: narration
    text: "Scorched plating shifted underfoot, groaning like a dying beast."
  - line: 397
    type: narration
    text: "Mika scanned the horizon—no sign of Geralt."
  - line: 398
    type: narration
    text: "Only devastation stretching to the distant, smoke-choked plains."
  - line: 400
    type: narration
    text: "From behind the line of soldiers, Oreck’s massive form broke through the haze, his scales streaked with soot."
  - line: 401
    type: narration
    text: "Two figures followed at his side—Kael and Roric—filthy, hollow-eyed, but upright."
  - line: 403
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“Commander,”"
  - line: 404
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck rumbled, voice carrying over the shifting metal. “These two survived the fall. No wounds, no burns. They were awake and moving before my scouts reached them.”"
  - line: 406
    type: narration
    text: "Mika studied them—slave markings still raw on their wrists, eyes too old for their years."
  - line: 407
    type: narration
    text: "“You’re lucky to be alive,” she said."
  - line: 408
    type: narration
    text: "“We could use that luck."
  - line: 409
    type: narration
    text: "Join us."
  - line: 410
    type: narration
    text: "Help clear the wounded, and you’ll have food and shelter with my unit.”"
  - line: 412
    type: narration
    text: "Roric hesitated, exchanging a look with Kael."
  - line: 413
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "“With respect, Commander,”"
  - line: 415
    type: narration
    text: "Kael nodded, voice barely above the wind."
  - line: 416
    type: narration
    text: "“We don’t belong in anyone’s army."
  - line: 417
    type: narration
    text: "Not anymore.”"
  - line: 419
    type: narration
    text: "Mika held their gaze for a long moment, then gave a short nod."
  - line: 420
    type: narration
    text: "“Then go."
  - line: 421
    type: narration
    text: "But remember—freedom’s a harder fight than war.”"
  - line: 423
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck watched them as they turned toward the distant ridge, the smoke curling between shattered cliffs like a birth shroud."
  - line: 424
    type: narration
    text: "“You think they’ll make it?” he asked."
  - line: 426
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Mika
    text: "“They’ll build something,”"
  - line: 428
    type: narration
    text: "> Oreck’s eyes lingered on the jagged remains of the hull."
  - line: 429
    type: narration
    text: "The plating still pulsed faintly, faint blue veins of Anunnaki power throbbing like a dying heart."
  - line: 431
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“Commander,”"
  - line: 432
    type: narration
    text: "he rumbled, voice lower now. “I served on vessels like this—before the rebellion. There are core chambers buried beneath the aft hull. If they’re still intact… they might be trying to wake something.”"
  - line: 434
    type: narration
    text: "Mika turned to him sharply."
  - line: 435
    type: narration
    text: "“You think the ship’s still alive?”"
  - line: 437
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "“Not alive,”"
  - line: 439
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“Go,”"
  - line: 440
    type: narration
    text: "Mika ordered. “Find out what it’s doing. Then find me.”"
  - line: 442
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck nodded once and descended into the molten ruins, his silhouette swallowed by the flickering blue light."
  - line: 444
    type: narration
    text: "As Oreck disappear into the crowd Roric and Kael disperse the other direction , Aldrin Sundrift  appeared suddenly, scrambling from a different rent in the hull."
  - line: 445
    type: narration
    text: "\"Commander!\" Aldrin panted, wiping grease from his brow."
  - line: 446
    type: narration
    text: "\"Found your husband's trail."
  - line: 447
    type: narration
    text: "A mysterious figure took five bodies toward Echo Tower."
  - line: 448
    type: narration
    text: "Said it was... urgent.\" His eyes darted nervously toward the continued path they came from."
  - line: 449
    type: narration
    text: "\"He wants to farm this graveyard."
  - line: 450
    type: narration
    text: "Madness.\""
  - line: 452
    type: narration
    text: "Mika's jaw tightened."
  - line: 453
    type: narration
    text: "Five bodies."
  - line: 454
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt's Five."
  - line: 455
    type: narration
    text: "But Geralt wasn't among them."
  - line: 456
    type: narration
    text: "Where was he?"
  - line: 457
    type: narration
    text: "\"One missing,\" she murmured, her voice tight."
  - line: 459
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Search this entire ruin,\""
  - line: 460
    type: narration
    text: "Mika commanded, her voice slicing through the metallic stink. \"Find where that tower is.\" Her soldiers fanned out, probing crevices, shouting names into echoing caverns of torn alloy."
  - line: 462
    type: narration
    text: "It was then that the Nephoretti  materialized silently beside Mika, their forms shimmering like heat haze."
  - line: 463
    type: narration
    text: "One pointed a translucent finger toward a narrow fissure choked with debris."
  - line: 464
    type: narration
    text: "\"The Echo breathes there,\" it whispered, its voice like wind through dry leaves."
  - line: 465
    type: narration
    text: "\"The Sage walks the thin places."
  - line: 466
    type: narration
    text: "Follow the blood that remembers.\""
  - line: 468
    type: narration
    text: "Blood remembers?"
  - line: 469
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt's cryptic tales flooded back – stories whispered in the dark about Nephoretti, beings woven from forgotten histories, who saw the world as layers of echoes."
  - line: 470
    type: narration
    text: "They spoke in riddles of 'blood memories,' ancestral imprints carried beyond death."
  - line: 471
    type: narration
    text: "Mika never understood it; it sounded like battlefield delirium."
  - line: 472
    type: narration
    text: "Yet here they were, pointing the way."
  - line: 473
    type: narration
    text: "Was Geralt's blood calling out?"
  - line: 474
    type: narration
    text: "Her own pulse hammered against her ribs, a drumbeat of dread and desperate hope."
  - line: 475
    type: narration
    text: "She plunged into the fissure, the Nephoretti dissolving into the fractured light behind her."
  - line: 477
    type: narration
    text: "The passage twisted sharply, narrowing until jagged rock scraped her shoulders."
  - line: 478
    type: narration
    text: "The shouts of her soldiers faded, replaced by a suffocating silence broken only by her ragged breath and the crunch of grit under her boots."
  - line: 479
    type: narration
    text: "Then, the air thickened."
  - line: 480
    type: narration
    text: "The rock walls seemed to ripple, their surfaces shifting subtly, like scales on a sleeping beast."
  - line: 481
    type: narration
    text: "The path ahead branched, then branched again – identical forks offering no clue."
  - line: 482
    type: narration
    text: "Mika paused, disoriented."
  - line: 483
    type: narration
    text: "Had she passed that oddly shaped stalactite before?"
  - line: 484
    type: narration
    text: "Twice?"
  - line: 485
    type: narration
    text: "Three times?"
  - line: 486
    type: narration
    text: "A cold sweat prickled her scalp."
  - line: 487
    type: narration
    text: "The fissure felt alive, breathing malice, warping space itself."
  - line: 488
    type: narration
    text: "Logic screamed retreat, but Geralt… he *had* to be deeper in."
  - line: 489
    type: narration
    text: "She pushed forward, choosing left, then right, guided only by a gnawing instinct deeper than the unnerving déjà vu."
  - line: 491
    type: narration
    text: "Her fingers traced the cold stone, seeking purchase, seeking sanity."
  - line: 492
    type: narration
    text: "Memories surfaced unbidden: Geralt’s laugh, rough and warm; the fierce pride in his eyes when the Five stood beside him; the chilling emptiness after Xal'Zirith’s touch."
  - line: 493
    type: narration
    text: "The grief, sharp and fresh despite the universe’s forgetting, clawed at her throat."
  - line: 494
    type: narration
    text: "Was this the tower’s doing?"
  - line: 495
    type: narration
    text: "Manipulating her fears?"
  - line: 496
    type: narration
    text: "Or was she simply unraveling?"
  - line: 497
    type: narration
    text: "She pressed her palm flat against the vibrating rock. *Find him."
  - line: 498
    type: narration
    text: "Just find him.* The mantra pulsed with her frantic heartbeat."
  - line: 499
    type: narration
    text: "She stumbled around another bend, blind to the passage’s unnatural symmetry, consumed by the desperate search within and without."
  - line: 501
    type: narration
    text: "Suddenly, the oppressive rock walls fell away."
  - line: 502
    type: narration
    text: "Mika staggered, blinking against harsh, unfiltered light."
  - line: 503
    type: narration
    text: "The cool, metallic stench of the wreckage vanished, replaced by dry, sterile heat."
  - line: 504
    type: narration
    text: "She stood on a barren plateau under a bruised sky, surrounded by jagged ridges of crimson rock that clawed at the horizon like broken teeth."
  - line: 505
    type: narration
    text: "Wind, hot and abrasive, scoured the dust, carrying the faint, metallic tang of distant ozone."
  - line: 506
    type: narration
    text: "Silence roared here, louder than the fissure’s whispers."
  - line: 507
    type: narration
    text: "Where was the tower?"
  - line: 508
    type: narration
    text: "Where was her army?"
  - line: 509
    type: narration
    text: "Panic flared – she’d wandered far beyond safety, lured deeper than she realized."
  - line: 510
    type: narration
    text: "This desolate expanse felt alien, wrong."
  - line: 511
    type: narration
    text: "Yet… a faint tremor in the air, a low hum vibrating through the soles of her boots, pulsed from somewhere ahead, beyond the nearest ridge."
  - line: 512
    type: narration
    text: "Power."
  - line: 513
    type: narration
    text: "Ancient power."
  - line: 514
    type: narration
    text: "Echo Tower."
  - line: 515
    type: narration
    text: "And Geralt?"
  - line: 516
    type: narration
    text: "Her gaze swept the desolation, heart hammering against her ribs."
  - line: 517
    type: narration
    text: "Nothing moved but dust devils swirling in the distance."
  - line: 519
    type: narration
    text: "A glint caught her eye near the base of the nearest ridge – not metal, but something darker, wetter."
  - line: 520
    type: narration
    text: "She scrambled down the scree slope, stones skittering beneath her."
  - line: 521
    type: narration
    text: "Half-buried in rust-colored sand lay a scrap of heavy, dark fabric, stiff with dried blood."
  - line: 522
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt’s cloak."
  - line: 523
    type: narration
    text: "Her breath hitched."
  - line: 524
    type: narration
    text: "He’d been here."
  - line: 525
    type: narration
    text: "Alive?"
  - line: 526
    type: narration
    text: "Captive?"
  - line: 527
    type: narration
    text: "She gripped the bloody cloth, its texture rough and familiar against her palm, a tangible anchor in the disorienting void."
  - line: 528
    type: narration
    text: "The low hum intensified, thrumming through her bones."
  - line: 529
    type: narration
    text: "Whatever lay beyond that ridge held answers."
  - line: 530
    type: narration
    text: "And Geralt."
  - line: 531
    type: narration
    text: "She followed the blood tracks, the desert sun glaring down on her solitary defiance."
  - line: 533
    type: narration
    text: "The crimson stains led her in a cruel, winding expedition across the plateau."
  - line: 534
    type: narration
    text: "They vanished abruptly at the sheer base of the ridge, only to reappear, impossibly, high above on its jagged summit."
  - line: 535
    type: narration
    text: "Was he dragged?"
  - line: 536
    type: narration
    text: "Flung?"
  - line: 537
    type: narration
    text: "How could so much blood stain this desolate land?"
  - line: 538
    type: narration
    text: "How much further must he be?"
  - line: 539
    type: narration
    text: "The sheer volume terrified her."
  - line: 540
    type: narration
    text: "Each step became a leaden weight."
  - line: 541
    type: narration
    text: "The oppressive heat pressed down, the bruised sky seeming to sag under its own despair."
  - line: 542
    type: narration
    text: "Exhaustion clawed at her."
  - line: 543
    type: narration
    text: "She stumbled, dropping to her knees in the coarse sand."
  - line: 544
    type: narration
    text: "The bloody scrap of cloak felt heavy in her fist."
  - line: 545
    type: narration
    text: "She wiped the stinging sweat from her brow with it, the coarse, dried blood gritting against her skin, leaving a stark, rust-brown smear across her forehead."
  - line: 546
    type: narration
    text: "His blood."
  - line: 547
    type: narration
    text: "Painting her."
  - line: 548
    type: narration
    text: "A grim benediction."
  - line: 549
    type: narration
    text: "The weight of the sky felt crushing."
  - line: 551
    type: narration
    text: "Then, a sharp cry pierced the heavy silence."
  - line: 552
    type: narration
    text: "Above, against the bruised expanse, a falcon circled."
  - line: 553
    type: narration
    text: "It screamed again, a piercing sound that cut through the oppressive hum."
  - line: 554
    type: narration
    text: "Another joined it, then another."
  - line: 555
    type: narration
    text: "Falcons."
  - line: 556
    type: narration
    text: "Three of them, riding the thermals rising from the heated rocks."
  - line: 557
    type: narration
    text: "They wheeled, then dipped sharply, skimming low over the ridge Mika had been heading towards."
  - line: 558
    type: narration
    text: "They vanished beyond its crest."
  - line: 559
    type: narration
    text: "Water?"
  - line: 560
    type: narration
    text: "Prey?"
  - line: 561
    type: narration
    text: "Or… Geralt?"
  - line: 562
    type: narration
    text: "Hope, fragile and fierce, surged."
  - line: 563
    type: narration
    text: "She pushed herself up, her legs protesting, the bloody cloth clutched tight."
  - line: 564
    type: narration
    text: "She scrambled up the treacherous slope, fingers scraping raw on sharp rock, following the falcons’ path."
  - line: 565
    type: narration
    text: "Maybe they’d lead her to water."
  - line: 566
    type: narration
    text: "Maybe, just maybe, to him."
  - line: 567
    type: narration
    text: "She crested the ridge, gasping."
  - line: 569
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"he\""
  - line: 570
    type: narration
    text: "? Her gaze swept the basin. Nothing moved but the dust devils. A dead shrub protruding out of the ridge above... Falcons nest.  Babys.  Not Geralt… her last conscious thought was his name, echoing emptily in her mind as the swirling dust, the oppressive heat, and the crushing weight of his absence finally overwhelmed her. She slumped forward, unconscious, her face pressed against the sand stained with only memory of him."
  - line: 572
    type: narration
    text: "Cold water splashed across Mika’s forehead, sharp and startling."
  - line: 573
    type: narration
    text: "She gasped, jerking upright, blinking against the sudden glare of torches."
  - line: 574
    type: narration
    text: "A figure knelt before her, silhouetted against the light, but it wasn't Aldrin."
  - line: 576
    type: narration
    text: "The face that swam into focus was Oreck’s, but it was framed by a cowl of iridescent, reptilian scales that seemed to drink the firelight."
  - line: 577
    type: narration
    text: "His simple slave’s tunic was gone, replaced by form-fitting armor of the same dark, segmented material, which emitted a low, almost sub-audible hum."
  - line: 578
    type: narration
    text: "Wrist-mounted gauntlets housed dormant, crystalline lenses, and his eyes, once familiar, now held a new, unsettling depth, as if he’d seen the blueprint of the world beneath its skin."
  - line: 580
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Oreck?\""
  - line: 581
    type: narration
    text: "Mika croaked, her mind struggling to reconcile the man with the machine."
  - line: 583
    type: narration
    text: "Relief washed over the faces of the soldiers crowding around them, but Oreck’s expression remained an unreadable mask of alien alloy and human concern."
  - line: 584
    type: narration
    text: "\"You fell too deep into the Echo,\" he said, his voice layered with a faint, harmonic resonance from his gear."
  - line: 585
    type: narration
    text: "\"It was trying to map your memories."
  - line: 586
    type: narration
    text: "I had to pull you back.\""
  - line: 588
    type: narration
    text: "The crushing weight of disappointment returned, heavier than before."
  - line: 589
    type: narration
    text: "Disappointment settled deep in her bones, colder than the plateau night air now biting through her cloak."
  - line: 590
    type: narration
    text: "He wasn't here."
  - line: 591
    type: narration
    text: "He’d vanished from this spot."
  - line: 592
    type: narration
    text: "Again."
  - line: 594
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"The trail,\""
  - line: 595
    type: narration
    text: "she demanded, her voice rough. \"Geralt's trail?\""
  - line: 597
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck shook his head, the motion fluid and silent."
  - line: 598
    type: narration
    text: "\"Only this.\" He gestured with a gauntleted hand toward the dried bloodstain nearby."
  - line: 599
    type: narration
    text: "\"And your tracks leading here."
  - line: 600
    type: narration
    text: "Alone.\""
  - line: 602
    type: narration
    text: "As Mika’s head cleared, Aldrin stepped forward, his eyes wide with a mixture of awe and fear as he looked at Oreck."
  - line: 603
    type: narration
    text: "\"He returned just as you collapsed, Commander."
  - line: 604
    type: narration
    text: "Came walking out of a fissure we didn't even see."
  - line: 605
    type: narration
    text: "And he brought... this.\" Aldrin held out a cracked slate tablet, its surface etched with angular symbols that now glowed with a soft, internal light, reacting to Oreck's presence."
  - line: 607
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck reached out, and the symbols on the tablet writhed, reconfiguring into a clear, sharp map."
  - line: 608
    type: narration
    text: "\"The Sage’s path is written."
  - line: 609
    type: narration
    text: "Not here,\" Oreck intoned, his new armor pulsing gently."
  - line: 610
    type: narration
    text: "\"The Echo Tower you seek… it lies elsewhere.\" His finger, clad in the dark metal, traced a symbol that burned brighter at his touch."
  - line: 611
    type: narration
    text: "\"Three hundred miles south."
  - line: 612
    type: narration
    text: "Where the Skyfire Peaks bite the Salt Flats.\""
  - line: 614
    type: narration
    text: "South."
  - line: 615
    type: narration
    text: "Three hundred miles."
  - line: 616
    type: narration
    text: "The distance felt immense, another cruel delay."
  - line: 617
    type: narration
    text: "Yet, the spark ignited beneath her despair."
  - line: 618
    type: narration
    text: "A destination."
  - line: 619
    type: narration
    text: "Answers."
  - line: 620
    type: narration
    text: "And now, a guide clad in the skin of the enemy."
  - line: 622
    type: narration
    text: "Mika straightened, brushing the grit from her palms."
  - line: 623
    type: narration
    text: "Her eyes met Oreck's strange, new gaze."
  - line: 624
    type: narration
    text: "\"Then we move south."
  - line: 625
    type: narration
    text: "Immediately.\" Her command was firm, her resolve locking into place."
  - line: 626
    type: narration
    text: "\"Oreck, you lead the way.\""
  - line: 628
    type: narration
    text: "The soldiers exchanged glances, then nodded, their resolve hardening."
  - line: 629
    type: narration
    text: "The hunt wasn't over; it had simply found a new, and far more strange, path."
  - line: 631
    type: internal_monologue
    text: "\"Born leader?\""
  - line: 632
    type: narration
    text: "she thought. *Or something the ship rewrote?* But his path was true, leading them swiftly away from the plateau's despair. For the first time since finding the bloodied cloak, Mika felt the tight knot in her chest loosen slightly. They were moving. They had a direction. Oreck was their key."
  - line: 634
    type: narration
    text: "They marched until the jagged Skyfire Peaks cast long, purple shadows across the desolate Salt Flats stretching southward."
  - line: 635
    type: narration
    text: "The air cooled rapidly, biting at exposed skin."
  - line: 636
    type: narration
    text: "Aldrin pointed to a shallow depression sheltered by wind-scoured sandstone pillars."
  - line: 637
    type: narration
    text: "\"Camp here, Commander?"
  - line: 638
    type: narration
    text: "Windbreak's decent.\" Mika nodded curtly."
  - line: 639
    type: narration
    text: "\"Make it quick and cold."
  - line: 640
    type: narration
    text: "No fires.\" The risk of detection was too high."
  - line: 641
    type: narration
    text: "Soldiers began unpacking rations and unfurling thin thermal blankets, the clatter of gear echoing softly in the gathering dusk."
  - line: 642
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck remained standing apart, facing south, his scaled cowl pulled low."
  - line: 643
    type: narration
    text: "The crystalline lenses in his gauntlets pulsed faintly, casting shifting blue patterns on the salt crust at his feet."
  - line: 645
    type: narration
    text: "Mika approached him, handing him a strip of dried ration meat."
  - line: 646
    type: narration
    text: "\"What do those lenses see?\" she asked quietly, nodding at the gauntlets."
  - line: 647
    type: narration
    text: "Her voice felt loud in the sudden quiet of camp setup."
  - line: 649
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck didn't turn."
  - line: 650
    type: narration
    text: "\"Residual energy trails,\" he murmured, the harmonic layer beneath his voice more pronounced."
  - line: 651
    type: narration
    text: "\"Like footprints in wet sand, but fading."
  - line: 652
    type: narration
    text: "The Sage..."
  - line: 653
    type: narration
    text: "Zephyr... his passage burns bright."
  - line: 654
    type: narration
    text: "Older than the mountains.\" He finally looked at her, his eyes catching the last of the twilight."
  - line: 655
    type: narration
    text: "\"The Five are with him."
  - line: 656
    type: narration
    text: "Their signatures are distinct."
  - line: 657
    type: narration
    text: "Faint\" He paused, the lenses dimming slightly."
  - line: 658
    type: narration
    text: "\"Geralt's trail... i cannot see.. but we will find him mika.. dont think about it too much.\""
  - line: 660
    type: narration
    text: "He finally bit into the ration, the movement precise."
  - line: 661
    type: narration
    text: "\"Rest while you can, Commander."
  - line: 662
    type: narration
    text: "Tomorrow, the Salt Flats."
  - line: 663
    type: narration
    text: "The ground remembers everything that crosses it."
  - line: 664
    type: narration
    text: "Especially things trying to hide.\" He turned back to the south, the blue light from his gauntlets flaring once, briefly illuminating the vast, silent expanse before them like a frozen sea under a bruised sky."
  - line: 665
    type: narration
    text: "The hum of his armor deepened, harmonizing with the rising night wind."
  - line: 667
    type: narration
    text: "end of chapter 033-the march"

